    "name": "Kiwi Berries",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Kiwi berries arebite-sized, smooth-skinned fruits (</span><i><em class=\"lexical-text-editor--italic\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Actinidia arguta</em></i><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">) that taste like sweet kiwis and can be eaten whole just like grapes.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Flavor</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: They taste very similar to standard kiwis, but they are often sweeter and more aromatic.</span></p><ul class=\"lexical-text-editor--list-ul\"><li value=\"1\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Vitamins</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: They are packed with Vitamin C and Vitamin E.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Minerals and Fiber</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: They provide high amounts of potassium, fiber, and antioxidants.</span></li></ul>",
